    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, i'm working on my lit review and getting super confused about citations. if i have a source with 4 or 5 authors, how do i do the in-text citation for APA 7th vs chicago? i keep mixing up when to use et al.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For APA 7th edition, when a source has three or more authors, you use the first author's last name followed by \"et al.\" for all citations, including the first one. In contrast, Chicago Style (Notes and Bibliography) usually lists the first few authors in the footnote for the first citation, and uses \"et al.\" in subsequent citations if there are many. Always double-check your required style guide as nuances can vary slightly between editions.",
